            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Ganita Manjari | Grade 9 | Part I"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "doc_title",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.373,
            0.113,
            0.622,
            0.143
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Exercise Set 6.3"
            }
          ],
          "level": 1
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.113,
            0.169,
            0.731,
            0.198
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Unless stated otherwise, use the approximation "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac { 2 2 } { 7 }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " for π."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.131,
            0.198,
            0.887,
            0.237
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "1. Find the area of a sector of a circle with radius 7 cm if the angle of the sector is "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "6 0 ^ { \\circ }"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.131,
            0.249,
            0.884,
            0.271
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "2. Find the area of a quadrant of a circle whose circumference is 44 cm."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.131,
            0.281,
            0.885,
            0.322
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "3. The length of the minute hand of a clock is 7 cm. Find the area swept by the minute hand in 10 minutes."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.13,
            0.333,
            0.886,
            0.413
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "4. A chord of a circle of radius 10 cm subtends "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "9 0 ^ { \\circ }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " at the centre. Find the area of the corresponding: (i) minor sector (that subtends "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "9 0 ^ { \\circ }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " at the centre), and (ii) major sector (that subtends "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "2 7 0 ^ { \\circ }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " at the centre). (Use "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\pi \\approx 3 . 1 4 . )"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.131,
            0.423,
            0.886,
            0.488
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "5. A chord of a circle of radius 15 cm subtends an angle of "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "6 0 ^ { \\circ }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " at the centre of the circle. Find the areas of the corresponding minor and major segments of the circle. (Use "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\pi \\approx 3 . 1 4"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\sqrt{3} \\approx 1.73.)"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.131,
            0.498,
            0.886,
            0.559
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "6. A car has two wipers which do not overlap. Each wiper has a blade of length 28 cm and sweeps through an angle of "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "1 2 0 ^ { \\bar { \\circ } }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " . Find the total area cleaned at each sweep of the blades."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.12,
            0.567,
            0.886,
            0.656
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "*7. A chord of a circle of radius r subtends an angle of "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "6 0 ^ { \\circ }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " at the centre of the circle. Show that the area of the corresponding minor "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\pi r^{2}\\Biggl(\\frac{1}{6}-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4}\\Biggr)"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.12,
            0.656,
            0.886,
            0.737
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "*8. An equilateral triangle is inscribed in a circle of radius r. Show that the ratio of the area of the triangle to the area of the circle is equal to "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac{3\\sqrt{3}}{4\\pi} \\approx 0.413"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.12,
            0.737,
            0.886,
            0.792
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "*9. A square is inscribed in a circle of radius r. Show that the ratio of the area of the square to the area of the circle is equal to "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac { 2 } { \\pi }   \\approx   0 . 6 3 7"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.113,
            0.795,
            0.886,
            0.899
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "*10. A hexagon is inscribed in a circle of radius r. Show that the ratio of the area of the hexagon to the area of the circle is equal to "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac { 3 \\sqrt { 3 } } { 2 \\pi }   \\approx   0 . 8 2 7"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " . Can you see why the answer is exactly twice the answer to Question 8?"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
